\description{
Reads the object \code{pheatmap::pheatmap()} returns as a \code{heat} layer
(\link{PheatmapHeatmapLayerProcessor}) and, for each side with a drawn
dendrogram, a \code{tree} layer (\link{PheatmapTreeLayerProcessor}), and draws its
\code{gtable} for the SVG. Experimental. Annotation tracks are not read.

\strong{Grid.} Each layer is a subplot placed where pheatmap draws it: the row
tree left of the matrix, the column tree above it, and nothing in the
corner above the row tree -- \verb{[[row tree, heat], [empty, column tree]]},
as far as each side is drawn. The grid's rows run \strong{bottom first}.
maidr.js does not measure this grid in the SVG -- it places a subplot
by its layer's first selector, which neither the heat layer's grid of
selectors nor the empty corner gives it -- so it orders it as written,
where the up arrow moves to the next row; written bottom first, up moves
from the matrix to the column tree above it, and the reader starts in
the bottom left subplot, the row tree.

When the cells' values cannot be read -- not drawn with \code{\link[=pheatmap]{pheatmap()}},
which keeps them, and with no legend (\code{legend = FALSE}) or one labelled
with words, and no numbers printed in the cells -- the chart falls back
to an image rather than being read without them.
}
